---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { GROUP_SHARING_DOC_PUBLISHED } from '../../../data/docsNav';

// LAUNCH GATE: group sharing is beta-only and not in the public release yet, so this
// page is hidden. Until GROUP_SHARING_DOC_PUBLISHED is flipped to true (in the release
// that ships group sharing), anyone hitting this URL is redirected to the docs home and
// the page is not linked from the nav. Flip the one flag in docsNav.ts to publish.
if (!GROUP_SHARING_DOC_PUBLISHED) {
  return Astro.redirect('/budgetbaby/docs');
}

const headings = [
  { id: 'what-it-is',     text: 'What group sharing is' },
  { id: 'requirements',   text: 'Requirements' },
  { id: 'cloud-sync',     text: 'Why Cloud Sync is required' },
  { id: 'setup',          text: 'Setting up a group' },
  { id: 'budget',         text: 'The group needs its own budget' },
  { id: 'splitting',      text: 'Assigning and splitting bills' },
  { id: 'settle-up',      text: 'Settle up' },
  { id: 'seats',          text: 'Seats and roles' },
  { id: 'troubleshooting', text: 'A member sees nothing' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Group Sharing"
  description="Share a budget with a partner or family in BudgetBaby. Requirements, how Cloud Sync moves data between devices, setting up the group budget, assigning and splitting bills, settle-up, seats and roles, and troubleshooting when a member sees nothing."
  canonical="/budgetbaby/docs/group-sharing"
  headings={headings}
>
  <div class="docs-content">
    <h1>Group Sharing</h1>
    <p class="docs-summary">
      Group sharing lets two or more people share one budget, split bills, and settle up.
      Because each person uses their own phone and their own account, group data travels
      between devices through the cloud. The single most important requirement is that
      Cloud Sync is on for every member, on every device.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what-it-is">What group sharing is</h2>
    <p>
      A group is a shared budget that more than one person can see and edit. The person who
      creates the group is the admin. They invite others, set up the group's budget, and assign
      or split bills so each member can see their own share. Members can record payments and
      mark their share settled. Your personal budget stays separate and private; a group is an
      additional, shared budget you switch into.
    </p>

    <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloud Sync on, for every member, on every device.</strong> This is how group data moves between phones. See the next section.</li>
      <li><strong>A group plan with a seat for each member who needs Premium access.</strong> Membership itself is free; a seat grants a member the Premium feature set. The group budget and a member's assigned share are visible without a seat.</li>
      <li><strong>The group has its own budget.</strong> A group does not inherit anyone's personal budget. The admin sets up a budget while switched into the group.</li>
      <li><strong>A connection.</strong> Changes made offline are saved on the device and sync to other members once you reconnect.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="cloud-sync">Why Cloud Sync is required</h2>
    <p>
      BudgetBaby is offline-first: your data lives on your device. Two phones never connect to
      each other directly. The only path between members is the cloud:
    </p>
    <pre class="docs-flow">Admin's phone  --upload-->  cloud  --download-->  Member's phone</pre>
    <p>
      With Cloud Sync turned off, the admin's group budget, bills, and splits never leave their
      phone, so other members have nothing to download and see an empty group. For this reason,
      BudgetBaby turns Cloud Sync on automatically when you create or join a group, and keeps it
      on while you are a member. If Cloud Sync is ever off, or a sync cannot complete, the app
      shows a banner in the group so you know your changes are not reaching other members yet.
    </p>

    <h2 id="setup">Setting up a group</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to Settings, then Group, and create a group (or join one with an invite code or QR link).</li>
      <li>Cloud Sync turns on automatically as part of creating or joining.</li>
      <li>Switch into the group from the budget switcher at the top of the Home screen. The group is listed under Groups.</li>
      <li>Invite members from the group screen using Invite a member.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="budget">The group needs its own budget</h2>
    <p>
      A common point of confusion: a group does not use your personal budget. After creating the
      group, switch into it from the budget switcher, and on the Home screen choose Set up your
      monthly budget. That budget belongs to the group and syncs to every member. Until the group
      has its own budget, members switched into the group will see No Budget Set.
    </p>

    <h2 id="splitting">Assigning and splitting bills</h2>
    <p>
      While switched into the group, open Settings, then Group, then Assign and split bills.
      Pick a bill and either assign the whole bill to one member or split it. Splits support
      four modes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Equal</strong> divides the bill evenly among the people you include.</li>
      <li><strong>Amounts</strong> lets you type each person's exact share; the shares must add up to the bill before you can save.</li>
      <li><strong>Percent</strong> divides by percentage; the percentages must total 100.</li>
      <li><strong>Shares</strong> divides by ratio, for example 2 to 1.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can choose who pays the bill to the vendor (the person everyone else reimburses), or
      leave it as the shared pool. Once saved, each member sees their own share on their Home and
      Bills screens.
    </p>

    <h2 id="settle-up">Settle up</h2>
    <p>
      Every member can open Your share and settle-up from the group screen to see what they owe,
      record a payment, and mark a share paid. Recording a payment notifies the person who is owed.
      The settle-up ledger is self-reported: members record their own payments, and only the person
      who made a payment can record it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="seats">Seats and roles</h2>
    <p>
      A group plan includes a number of seats (Pair includes two, Family includes more). The admin
      assigns seats from Manage seats. A member can request a seat, and the admin approves it there.
      A member without a seat is still a full member and can see the group budget and their assigned
      share; a seat adds the Premium feature set for that member. Roles are admin, member, and a
      read-only viewer. Admin-only actions include setting up the group budget, assigning and
      splitting bills, and managing seats.
    </p>

    <h2 id="troubleshooting">A member sees nothing</h2>
    <p>
      If a member is in the group but sees no budget or bills, check these in order:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloud Sync is on for both people.</strong> The admin needs it on to upload; the member needs it on to download. This is the most common cause. The group screen shows a banner when Cloud Sync is off or a sync has not completed.</li>
      <li><strong>The group has its own budget.</strong> If the admin only set up a personal budget, the group is empty. Switch into the group and set up the group's budget.</li>
      <li><strong>Both devices are online.</strong> Offline changes sync once you reconnect.</li>
      <li><strong>The member has switched into the group.</strong> Use the budget switcher at the top of Home and select the group under Groups.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      After the admin's changes have synced, the member can switch into the group and will see the
      group budget and their assigned share.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
